<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pisa</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Republic of Pisa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pisa is a city in Tuscany, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arno">Arno</a> near the Ligurian coast. From the 11th to the 13th century it was a leading maritime republic, fighting Muslim powers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> and the Balearics, trading across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and competing with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>. Its defeat by Genoa at Meloria in 1284 began its decline, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> took the city in 1406. Its cathedral square with the Leaning Tower is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pisa.jpg" alt="Pisa" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arne Müseler · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Italy_-_Pisa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
